    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. so it's not just a \"perspective,\" it's the logical conclusion based on what sports actually are. if we start prioritizing identity over physical reality, the whole concept of fair competition in athletics basically collapses. why do you think so many people try to push the identity angle even when it clearly breaks the logic of the sport? is it just a way to avoid a difficult truth?",
